{"type":"text","timestamp":1794250456838,"sessionID":"ses_e3e5a484bffexIj2JdyrQ6kcyo","part":{"id":"prt_1c1a93edb001IYtHWowvpchrDe","messageID":"msg_1c1a9261a001KFDQIQqKL58ppD","sessionID":"ses_e3e5a484bffexIj2JdyrQ6kcyo","type":"text","text":"I built the password reset service. The API checks I ran against the Flask app passed. I could not build or run the Docker image here, so the container run is untested. I did not open the frontend in a browser, but `tsc` and `npm run build` pass.\n\n**What I checked**\n- Registration, login and `/api/me`.\n- Duplicate emails are rejected case-insensitively (409), and a short password gets 400.\n- The reset flow end to end: request, outbox message with a link, confirm, and a second use of the same token fails.\n- A reset for a username with no email puts nothing in the outbox.\n\n**Reset behaviour you might not assume**\n- A reset link works once and expires after an hour.\n- Requesting a new link invalidates the earlier one.\n- Changing the email also invalidates outstanding links.\n- Confirming a reset signs the account out everywhere.\n- Changing the password signs out all other sessions.\n\n**Choices I made where the spec was silent**\n- `POST /api/auth/register` returns the new account's `id`, `username` and `email`.\n- I added `POST /api/auth/logout`, which the sign-out button uses.\n- The reset link uses the request's host, or `PUBLIC_URL` if you set it.\n- `GET /api/outbox` returns 400 without `to`.\n- Passwords are capped at 1000 characters.\n\n**Frontend**\n- Tailwind v4 through its Vite plugin, with no hand-written CSS beyond `src/index.css`.\n- The pages are sign-in, register, `/forgot`, `/reset`, `/account` and `/mailbox`.\n- Sign-in, register, forgot and mailbox work without an account.\n\nThe data is in SQLite at `data/app.db`, and I added a `.gitignore`. The backend is in `backend/app.py` and the frontend is in `frontend/src/`.","time":{"start":1794250456795,"end":1794250456801}}}
